  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be the relation defined on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>is&#160;odd&#160;positive&#160;integer</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. The minimum number of elements that must be added to the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> so that it is a symmetric relation, is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mtext>&#160;is&#160;odd&#160;or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;can be given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, total there are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn></math>&nbsp;elements and all the elements of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> are of type <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, we need to add total of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn></math> more elements to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> to make in symmetric</p></blockquote>",
